Problem description
- The company must choose a subset of candidates from a candidate pool $$\mathcal{C}$$ to form an R&D team.
- Each candidate $$i \in \mathcal{C}$$ has three attributes: salary requirement $$s_i$$, skill level $$u_i$$, and project management experience $$e_i$$.
- The hiring decision is a single-stage planning decision over the horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$, with no multi-period carryover.
- The planning goal is to select candidates so that the total salary paid is as small as possible while satisfying all hiring requirements.
- The total salary of all hired candidates must not exceed the available budget $$B$$.
- The number of hired candidates must not exceed the hiring limit $$H^{\max}$$.
- The total skill level of the hired candidates must be at least the required minimum $$U^{\min}$$.
- The total project management experience of the hired candidates must be at least the required minimum $$E^{\min}$$.
- For every incompatible pair in the set $$\mathcal{K}$$, at most one candidate from that pair may be hired.
- A solution is represented by:
  - A binary decision variable $$x_i$$ for each candidate $$i \in \mathcal{C}$$, where $$x_i=1$$ means candidate $$i$$ is hired and $$x_i=0$$ means candidate $$i$$ is not hired.
  - The selected team as the subset of candidates with $$x_i=1$$.
  - The resulting total salary, total skill, and total experience of the selected team as derived quantities.

Input Format
{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "$$i$$",
      "salary_requirement": "$$s_i$$",
      "skill_level": "$$u_i$$",
      "project_management_experience": "$$e_i$$"
    }
  ],
  "budget": "$$B$$",
  "max_hires": "$$H^{\\max}$$",
  "minimum_total_skill": "$$U^{\\min}$$",
  "minimum_total_experience": "$$E^{\\min}$$",
  "incompatible_pairs": [
    {
      "candidate_a": "$$i$$",
      "candidate_b": "$$j$$"
    }
  ]
}
The candidate attribute arrays have length $$N=|\mathcal{C}|$$, and the incompatible pair list is the set $$\mathcal{K}$$ of forbidden candidate pairings.

Output Format
{
  "hire_decisions": [
    {
      "candidate_id": "$$i$$",
      "selected": "$$x_i$$"
    }
  ],
  "selected_candidates": [
    "$$i \\in \\mathcal{C}: x_i=1$$"
  ],
  "total_salary": "$$Z_s$$",
  "total_skill": "$$Z_u$$",
  "total_experience": "$$Z_e$$"
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "F",
      "salary_requirement": 12000,
      "skill_level": 2,
      "project_management_experience": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "G",
      "salary_requirement": 15000,
      "skill_level": 3,
      "project_management_experience": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "H",
      "salary_requirement": 18000,
      "skill_level": 4,
      "project_management_experience": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "I",
      "salary_requirement": 5000,
      "skill_level": 1,
      "project_management_experience": 5
    },
    {
      "id": "J",
      "salary_requirement": 10000,
      "skill_level": 2,
      "project_management_experience": 4
    }
  ],
  "budget": 40000,
  "max_hires": 4,
  "minimum_total_skill": 8,
  "minimum_total_experience": 8,
  "incompatible_pairs": [
    {
      "candidate_a": "G",
